<title>NEW ZEALAND: Northland sees improvement in 2nd half.</title>
<headline>Northland sees improvement in 2nd half.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Northland Port Corp (NZ) Ltd said on Friday it expected an improvement in its results for the second six months of the year.</p>
<p>The company reported a 26.5 percent drop in net profit for the six months to March 31, 1997, to NZ$3.12 million from $4.25 million in the same period last year.</p>
<p>&quot;An improvement is expected in the second six months although this is likely to be below original budget,&quot; chairman Jim Hardie said.</p>
<p>--Wellington Newsroom (64 4) 4734746</p>
</text>
